    fix(QA-DUCKBRAIN-003): unlink O_DIRECT residue + surface DURABILITY_* codes in HTTP envelope
    
    appendJsonlDirect opened the target with O_CREAT before the O_DIRECT check,
    so a rejected open/write left the freshly-created current.jsonl behind as an
    empty file. Now the failure path unlinks the created target (only when this
    call would have created it — pre-existing files are never touched) and
    rethrows the durability error unchanged.
    
    DurabilityError is not an ApiError, so the shared errorHandler fell through
    to the generic 500 INTERNAL_ERROR and the machine-readable DURABILITY_* code
    was lost from every HTTP response. Added an isDurabilityError branch that
    emits {error, code} at status 500 (SUPA-1: durability failures fail LOUD —
    never downgraded to 4xx).
    
    Tests: +2 residue tests incl. pre-existing-file negative control (RED on
    pre-fix tree, GREEN post); +5 errorHandler envelope tests (3/5 RED pre-fix);
    http-durability envelope assertions extended. Suite 193/1539 -> 194/1547,
    AGENTS.md count lines synced. Verified foreman-side: red-proofs via stash
    controls, touched suites green solo, tsc clean, prettier tree-wide clean.
